		{
			"id": "hub",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "CAT8 — Tool friction, switching, and cost\nRQ3 · finding",
			"x": 140,
			"y": -80,
			"width": 400,
			"height": 100,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "cases",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Cases\nL1 L2 L4 S1 S3 S6 S7 S8 S9",
			"x": -220,
			"y": -80,
			"width": 300,
			"height": 70,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "code_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Codes** (29) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[L1-C17]] — prefers modelling tools over generic drawing tools\n- [[L1-C18]] — tool licensing pushes lecturer to switch tools\n- [[L1-C20]] — wants more tool time and examples in class\n- [[L1-C21]] — ideal tool would give feedback and next steps\n- [[L2-C11]] — code-generating tools motivate code-focused students\n- [[L2-C12]] — typed tools block mistakes and improve model quality\n- [[L2-C13]] — one multi-diagram tool reduces tool switching\n- [[L4-C16]] — expensive tools limit access and integration\n- [[L4-C26]] — missing integrated tools drives whiteboard use\n- [[L4-C27]] — piStar semantic checking is valued for iStar\n- [[L4-C28]] — switching tools across families creates friction\n- [[L4-C29]] — wants lightweight integrated cross-paradigm tool\n- [[S1-C08]] — tool options overwhelming for simple relations\n- [[S1-C20]] — fewer tool options make drawing easier\n- [[S3-C14]] — Bizagi vocabulary in UI helped learning\n- [[S3-C15]] — tool hover hints helped beginners start\n- [[S3-C16]] — large diagrams slow and can corrupt on save\n- [[S6-C04]] — worked examples set acceptable abstraction levels\n- [[S6-C12]] — separate tools and missed tutorial blocked NFR progress\n- [[S7-C06]] — exams judged by a homemade list and faith\n- [[S7-C07]] — class treats the teacher’s model as the right one\n- [[S7-C08]] — antique compile tool created more problems\n- [[S8-C02]] — ungraded exercises rarely checked unless you ask\n- [[S8-C05]] — skipped semantic tools and used draw.io\n- [[S8-C06]] — walk-around feedback almost always meant changes\n- [[S8-C07]] — shares with friends not course-group strangers\n- [[S9-C04]] — good enough when nothing is left to change\n- [[S9-C05]] — would hide poor drawing not a wrong model\n- [[S9-C06]] — archaic UML tool slower than paper but better than drawing",
			"x": 580,
			"y": 180,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 892,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "memo_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Memos** (9) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S1M4]] — simpler tools reduce option overwhelm\n- [[S3M4]] — Bizagi scaffolds vocabulary and syntax\n- [[S6M3]] — examples and attendance carry abstraction norms\n- [[L1M5]] — proper tools versus draw.io in teaching stance\n- [[L4M5]] — whiteboard compensates for missing integrated tools\n- [[L2M3]] — tools motivate through code and guardrails\n- [[S7M2]] — labs are gut feeling; exams are going on faith\n- [[S8M2]] — ungraded practice makes checking optional\n- [[S9M2]] — drawing skill and old tools shape sharing more than correctness",
			"x": -380,
			"y": 180,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 332,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "explainer",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "What this means\n\nTools also create pain: too many options, licence limits, mid-course switches, and antique or slow UIs. Students may drop a checker or skip a semantic suite when a simpler drawing tool already gets the work done.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": -340,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "1"
		}
	],
